# Creating Three Column Grids in CSS

Three columns provide excellent whitespace organization and still offer good mobile scalability.

## Pure CSS Three Column Layout

```st-pretty-code
# Create equal 33% columns
.container::before {
  content: '';
  visibility: hidden;
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 5em;
  outline: 0.5em solid transparent;
}

# Use CSS table layout for perfect alignment
.grid-table {
  display: table;
  width: 100%;
  table-layout: fixed;
}

.grid-row {
  display: table-row;
}

.grid-cell {
  position: relative;
  display: table-cell;
  padding: 20px 15px;
}

# Responsive adjustments
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .grid-row:nth-child(4n+1) .grid-cell:nth-child(3),
  .grid-row:nth-child(4n+2) .grid-cell:nth-child(3),
  .grid-row:nth-child(4n+3) { display: none !important }
}

@media (max viewing-angle: 60deg) {
  .grid-cell::before {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    content: ''
  }
}
```

